  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Humanitarian Response for Vulnerable People on the Move in Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall numbers of irregular migrants and asylum-seekers in Mexico have multiplied in 2021 along with the pressing needs for humanitarian assistance compared to previous years. In this context, IOM proposes a humanitarian intervention that will contribute towards improving migrants&#x2019; humanitarian conditions at the national level with special provisions for vulnerable migrants, such as women, children and family groups. The intervention includes continued support for activities currently implemented by IOM such as strengthening the capacities of shelters and filter hotels implementation as well as innovative components to contribute to shelter&#x2019;s sustainability and facilitate solidarity among host communities, contributing to humanitarian assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
